  "hypothesis": "Ordinary earned practice must trigger eligibility at its threshold and persist when level loss removes slots then gain restores one.",
  "expectedBehavior": "Six successes give18 practice without notification; seven give21 and spell-skill notification. Slot loss/regain preserves practice and emits the general notification.",
  "observedBehavior": "Three full C/JS matches; six/seven healthy cure-sickness successes, four failures, specific then general eligibility messages in order. JS verifies18/21 practice and19/1 free slots.",
  "witness": {
    "kind": "public_recording",
    "scope": "Ordinary known spell casts on a healthy Wizard; wizard-assisted resource setup and level loss/regain.",
    "limitations": [
      "Practice is earned by ordinary casts; level history is wizard-assisted and does not qualify natural Welcome back.",
      "C practice and slot values inferred from successful-cast messages and source; exact internal values separately asserted in JS.",
      "No skill advancement selection or refund of a naturally spent slot exercised in this package.",
      "Healthy cure-sickness branch only: no object-effect emulation, active sickness/sliming, combat or status-expiry path."
    ]
  },
